**Theorem 6: Obstacles Are Structural**

| Obstacle | Description | Why It Persists |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Economic dependency | The West benefits from colonization | It is profitable |
| Political power | The West dominates global institutions | It is powerful |
| Cultural assumption | The West believes it is the center | It is ingrained |
| Epistemic violence | The West dismisses other knowledge | It is self-reinforcing |
| Fear of loss | The West fears losing dominance | It is ego-driven |

**Corollary 6: The Obstacles Are Self-Reinforcing**

\[
\text{Obstacle} \to \text{More Colonization} \to \text{More Obstacle}
\]

The West colonizes because it is powerful. It is powerful because it colonizes. The cycle is self-reinforcing.

